# identify: reading parts' markings with the microscope (decision C12):
# the resistor's bands, the LED's color and the chip's number in the tray, read as the
# scope's picture gives them; the capacitor lies with its printed face
# sideways and cannot be read, so arm A puts it in the vise and the
# positioner tilts it toward the scope: at 30 degrees the face is seen
# too obliquely and the code may be misread (a warning); at 45 it reads.
reset circuit=demo
identify R1 mode=sensed
identify D1 mode=sensed
identify U1 mode=sensed
identify C1 mode=sensed
tool A tweezers
pick A C1 grasp=body
place A C1 at=0,0,-20
vise close
release A C1
lift A mm=60
stage tilt=30
identify C1 mode=sensed
stage tilt=45
identify C1 mode=sensed
